  "id": "Hackney-2025_2423",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "1.\tReplacing the existing 1960’s felt and woodwool flat roof in marine ply decking in traditional lead, repairs to roof timbers and re-slating the south-facing School roof including the conical tower roof and associated curved box gutter.\n\n2.\tDrainage, brickwork and stonework repairs to settlement cracking caused to various sections of the underground drainage system and drains within the entire St Columba’s Complex. These resulting failures are causing cracks to the east elevation archway next to the clergy house, the Mortuary Chapel SE Flèche (spire), and brickwork to the Link Building east archway.\n",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this consent.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 18(a) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990 as amended.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>"
  ],
